#{\footnote # recording}${\footnote $ Recording a Macro}K{\footnote K Recording a Macro}+{\footnote + procedures:010}
\pard\sb120\sa120\li120{\b\fs28 Recording a Macro}\par
\pard\li120\sa60\sb60{\b To record a macro}\par
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa60 1.\tab From the Macro menu, choose Record.\par
2.\tab Type its name and a shortcut key, and choose Start.\par
3.\tab Do what the macro is to repeat.\par
4.\tab Press CTRL+BREAK (or click Recorder's icon) and choose to save the macro.\par
\page
#{\footnote # playing}${\footnote $ Playing Back a Macro}K{\footnote K Playing Back a Macro}+{\footnote + procedures:020}
\pard\sb120\sa120\li120{\b\fs28 Playing Back a Macro}\par
\pard\li120\sa120 Press its shortcut key, or select it in Recorder's list and choose Run from the Macro menu.\par
\page
